<title>SINGAPORE: Singapura Building net up to S$5.8 mln.</title>
<headline>Singapura Building net up to S$5.8 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		  5.83	vs	3.67</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)    11.90	vs	7.60</p>
<p>    Dividend  (percent)     6.00	vs	4.00</p>
<p>    Operating income	 22.74	vs     21.89</p>
<p>    Investment income	 0.05	vs	0.07</p>
<p>    Other income		0.42	vs	0.51</p>
<p>    Pretax operating profit 8.32	vs	6.07</p>
<p>    Interest on borrowings  0.02	vs	0.01</p>
<p>    Interest on deposits    7.32	vs	8.23</p>
<p>    Taxation		    2.49	vs	2.40</p>
<p>Div payable/div register  Nov 8/Oct 28</p>
<p>NOTE: Singapura Building Society Ltd said rising costs, coupled with intense competition will put further pressure on profit margins. -- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
